🚨 severity: BLOCKING —
🚨 **BLOCKING: CI red — CRAP ratchet exceeded on both `backstopBridgeMocks` builders**

The `crap` check fails on head `47854b8a` (ci_failures.md; ci_failures_full.log):

```text
NEW > 8  js/unit-tests/test_mergeBot.js::backstopBridgeMocks: 9
NEW > 8  js/unit-tests/test_mergeTrigger.js::backstopBridgeMocks: 9
0 regression(s), 2 new over threshold, 0 improvement(s), 0 removed
##[error]Process completed with exit code 2.
```

The `resolveFailIds` branch added inside the `github_resolve_pr_thread` mock pushes the
`backstopBridgeMocks` builder over the CRAP 8 threshold in **both** test files. (The PR
description's "all new functions ≤ 8" holds for mergeBackstop.js, but the ratchet also
covers these modified test builders.)

Fix with the repo's own precedent — a named mock builder, exactly like `checkRunsPayload`
in this file ("gh-1200 precedent: named mock builders"):

```js
function resolveThreadMock(opts, calls) {
    return function (a) {
        if ((opts.resolveFailIds || []).indexOf(String(a.threadId)) !== -1) {
            throw new Error('422 ' + a.threadId);
        }
        calls.threadResolves.push(a);
        return '{}';
    };
}
// in backstopBridgeMocks:
github_resolve_pr_thread: resolveThreadMock(opts, calls),
```

Apply the identical extraction in `js/unit-tests/test_mergeTrigger.js` (its builder copy
is flagged at the same threshold). Unit tests themselves are green (verified locally:
63 + 139 passed) — this gate is the only red check.

